      "red_goal",
      "blue_goal"
    ],
    "output_semantics": "Each unnormalized slot is [alpha, residual_x_m, residual_y_m, residual_z_m, world_rotation_6d(6), gripper]. At chunk sampling, b is the selected causal blue position and g is blue_goal. The world TCP position is b + clip(alpha,0,1)*(g-b) + residual. Label alpha is the clipped 3-D orthogonal projection of the demonstrated commanded TCP position onto the b-to-g segment; when squared endpoint separation is at most 1e-4 m^2, alpha is defined as 1. Rotation is world aligned and projected from 6-D to SO(3). Gripper retains demonstrated scalar/sign semantics. Slot 0 is t-1 and execution uses slots 1..8 for t..t+7. decode_action calls panda_kinematics.solve_ik from freshly measured joints.",
    "parameter_semantics": "source_object selects the causally observed blue_pose position b in world metres; destination_field selects the calibrated blue_goal position g in world metres. The selected endpoints are resolved and frozen at each chunk replan. They are semantic frame selectors, not arbitrary coordinates or actuator commands.",
